{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.md","line":61,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex#lem:dc-ch9-2-3","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#cor:dc-ch3-3-9]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3","line":129,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[minimizing geodesics minimize energy]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch9-2-3}\n\n  \\uses{cor:dc-ch3-3-9, lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.3}\n  Let $p,q\\in M$ and let $\\gamma:[0,a]\\to M$ be a minimizing geodesic joining $p$ to\n  $q$. Then, for all curves $c:[0,a]\\to M$ joining $p$ to $q$,\n\n  $$\n  E(\\gamma)\\le E(c)\n  $$\n\n  with equality holding if and only if $c$ is a minimizing geodesic.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  $$\n  aE(\\gamma)=(L(\\gamma))^2\\le(L(c))^2\\le aE(c),\n  $$\n\n  which proves the first assertion. If equality holds, then $(L(c))^2=aE(c)$, so the\n  parameter of $c$ is proportional to arc length, and $L(\\gamma)=L(c)$, so $c$ is a\n  minimizing geodesic (see \\cref{cor:dc-ch3-3-9}). The converse is obvious.\n\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[minimizing geodesics minimize energy] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368392d322d33\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23cor%3Adc-ch3-3-9\">↗ cor:dc-ch3-3-9</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-3-inequality\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-3-equality-case\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch9:2.3</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p,q\\in M$\">$p,q\\in M$</span> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$</span> be a minimizing geodesic joining <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span>. Then, for all curves <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c:[0,a]\\to M$\">$c:[0,a]\\to M$</span> joining <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span>, <p></p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  E(\\gamma )\\le E(c)  \\]\">\\[  E(\\gamma )\\le E(c)  \\]</span> <p></p>with equality holding if and only if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is a minimizing geodesic.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  aE(\\gamma )=(L(\\gamma ))^2\\le (L(c))^2\\le aE(c),  \\]\">\\[  aE(\\gamma )=(L(\\gamma ))^2\\le (L(c))^2\\le aE(c),  \\]</span></p><p>which proves the first assertion. If equality holds, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(L(c))^2=aE(c)$\">$(L(c))^2=aE(c)$</span>, so the parameter of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is proportional to arc length, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L(\\gamma )=L(c)$\">$L(\\gamma )=L(c)$</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is a minimizing geodesic (see <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23cor%3Adc-ch3-3-9\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#cor:dc-ch3-3-9\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-636f723a64632d6368332d332d39\">item cor:dc-ch3-3-9</a>). The converse is obvious. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#cor:dc-ch3-3-9","title":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9","label":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#thm:dc-ch9-3-1","title":"thm:dc-ch9-3-1","label":"thm:dc-ch9-3-1"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[minimizing geodesics minimize energy]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch9-2-3}\n\n  \\uses{cor:dc-ch3-3-9, lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge, lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.3}\n  Let $p,q\\in M$ and let $\\gamma:[0,a]\\to M$ be a minimizing geodesic joining $p$ to\n  $q$. Then, for all curves $c:[0,a]\\to M$ joining $p$ to $q$,\n\n  $$\n  E(\\gamma)\\le E(c)\n  $$\n\n  with equality holding if and only if $c$ is a minimizing geodesic.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  $$\n  aE(\\gamma)=(L(\\gamma))^2\\le(L(c))^2\\le aE(c),\n  $$\n\n  which proves the first assertion. If equality holds, then $(L(c))^2=aE(c)$, so the\n  parameter of $c$ is proportional to arc length, and $L(\\gamma)=L(c)$, so $c$ is a\n  minimizing geodesic (see \\cref{cor:dc-ch3-3-9}). The converse is obvious.\n\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#cor:dc-ch3-3-9","title":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-pointwise-arclength","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}